# Project Standards

## Git — hard boundary

- **NEVER commit, push, tag, or amend.** The user runs all git commits themselves.
  Suggest a commit message when asked; do not run `git commit` even if asked to
  "wrap up" or "finish".
- Branch creation/switching only when the user explicitly directs it.

## Code quality

- **DRY**: one script/function per job; extract shared logic instead of copying
  (e.g. `scripts/sync_gdocs.py` replaced three near-identical download scripts).
- **Single responsibility, minimal footprint**: no dead code, unused imports,
  speculative options, or half-finished stubs.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. No commented-out code.

## Tooling

- Python deps via `uv` only (`uv add`, `uv add --group dev`, `uv run`). Never raw pip.
- After code changes: `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run ruff format .` — fix new
  errors before finishing.
- After docs/config changes: `uv run zensical build --strict` must pass.

## Generated content

- Pages starting with `<!-- AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/sync_gdocs.py -->` are built
  from Google Docs. Never hand-edit them — fix the source doc, the registry sheet,
  or the sync script, then re-run the sync.
- `docs/**/img/` and `docs/assets/pdfs/` are sync outputs; don't edit files there.
